{"dugong":{"id":"74515ba9-7295-418e-8871-f0a5acfea37d","word":"dugong","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Dugong dugon","tags":["masculine"],"word":"dugongo"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The Ceylong dugong is an extraordinary and interesting animal which is often seen on the coast. It is plentiful in and about the Gulf of Manaar, and resembles somewhat a huge, thickly-made, bluff-headed seal.","ref":"1914, Marcus W. Millett, Jungle Sport in Ceylon from Elephant to Snipe, page 84:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[12,18]],"id":"5e43f91e-060a-47a9-9237-e866920048c0"},{"text":"“What are those things that aren’t seals? Much worse than seals. Big, blubbery things. Dugongs.”","ref":"1988, Douglas Adams, The Long Dark Tea-Time of the Soul, William Heinemann Ltd, page 37:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[87,94]],"id":"a708fc39-8a04-4d3d-9be7-87e4fc80ddc8"}],"wikidata":["Q129544"],"senseid":["en:Q129544"],"links":[["sirenian","sirenian"],["Dugong dugon","Dugong dugon#Translingual"],["fluke","fluke#Etymology 3"]],"hypernyms":[{"word":"dugongid"},{"word":"dugong"},{"word":"sea cow"},{"word":"sirenian"},{"word":"marine mammal"},{"word":"mammal"},{"word":"vertebrate"},{"word":"animal"},{"word":"organism"},{"word":"creature"}],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"manatee","english":"fellow sirenian","translation":"fellow sirenian"},{"word":";","english":"fellow marine mammals","translation":"fellow marine mammals"},{"word":"whale"},{"word":"dolphin"},{"word":"walrus"},{"word":"seal"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["A plant-eating sirenian of the species Dugong dugon, found in tropical regions and having a fluked tail."],"id":"b71e7167-e181-4009-9874-e307f3ef36a3"},{"wikidata":["Q838603"],"senseid":["en:Q838603"],"links":[["Dugongidae","Dugongidae#Translingual"],["monotypic","monotypic"],["Dugong","Dugong#Translingual"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"dugongid"}],"hypernyms":[{"word":"sea cow